  "configuration_id": "config_030",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only models dominate (best: scvi_n200 + multiprofile + avgpool/transformer at ~0.65), while image-only models are very weak (ResNet50: 0.208, ViT-L: 0.227). The critical open question is whether the weak image signal provides any complementary information when fused with the strong RNA representation. This experiment pairs the best-validated RNA configuration (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool) with the simplest image encoder (ResNet50) and simplest fusion (concat), forming a clean comparison against config_005 (0.650) and config_006 (0.653). If config_030 fails to exceed ~0.65, it strongly suggests image adds no value and we can eliminate all 36 multimodal configs, redirecting budget to RNA-only refinement. If it does exceed, it validates pursuing multimodal fusion and motivates testing weighted fusion and ViT-L. This is the highest-information experiment because it resolves the single most consequential design decision (unimodal vs. multimodal) with minimal confounding changes."
}

